## shared_media_placeholder_adoption

### Current Progress
- **Phase 0: Repository media inventory and exception policy** - ✅ Complete
- **Phase 1: Shared primitive contract hardening** - ✅ Complete
- **Phase 2: Page content and rich-text migration** - ✅ Complete
- **Phase 3: Forum, uploads, inbox, and previews migration** - ✅ Complete
- **Phase 4: Commerce migration** - ✅ Complete
- **Phase 5: Profile, branding, security, and thumbnails migration** - ✅ Complete
- **Phase 6: Enforcement, documentation, and audit** - ✅ Complete

### Inventory Basis
- 2026-08-16: source scan found 63 direct image/video/audio elements in 31 production TSX files after excluding the shared primitive and tests.
- 2026-08-16: reviewed generated rich-text media, dynamic image/video backgrounds, configured branding, favicon metadata, YouTube thumbnails/player, Leaflet markers, avatar fallback, MediaStream playback, and canvas/export paths.
- 2026-08-16: the existing primitive/article baseline passed 7 focused tests and the frontend production build before this planning pass.
- 2026-08-16: todo pairing, status vocabulary, linked-file, duplicate-topic, and diff checks passed.

### Implementation Evidence
- 2026-08-16: hardened `MediaPlaceholder` with typed layout/fit/playback/frame,
  caller class/style, media-ref, and lifecycle callbacks; URL-keyed remounting and
  current-URL event guards prevent stale ready/error transitions.
- 2026-08-16: migrated page component renderers, card parts, hero backgrounds,
  event/image cards, galleries, and profile banners. Profile avatars now use the
  compact `UserAvatar` exception; hero video cycling, tint layers, and controls
  remain intact.
- 2026-08-16: replaced the disabled TipTap read-only instance with the sanitized
  `RichTextRenderer` adapter. Authored image/video/audio tags now use the shared
  lifecycle without mutating serialized HTML; editable TipTap documents are
  unchanged.
- 2026-08-16: added `npm run check:media-placeholders` with exact reviewed counts
  and reasons for remaining migration surfaces and durable native-media
  exceptions. Phase migrations must shrink or remove those entries.
- 2026-08-16: migrated upload grid/list thumbnails, inbox attachments,
  media-scraper thumbnails, and all preview paths. The shared lightbox now uses a
  native modal lifecycle, restores focus, supports Escape/arrow keys, and keeps
  close/cycle controls available after media failure.
- 2026-08-16: migrated product cards/details, similar-product thumbnails, product
  media administration, cart/order thumbnails, and the legacy image lightbox.
  Failed covers do not block preview, add-to-cart, quantity, remove, or media
  deletion actions.
- 2026-08-16: removed every Phase 3 and Phase 4 entry from the exact-count
  enforcement allowlist; remaining entries are Phase 5 work or durable native
  exceptions.
- 2026-08-16: migrated TOTP QR codes, profile/banner/card-art/settings previews,
  configured header/footer branding, mention avatars, YouTube thumbnails, and
  captured stream stills. Hidden/live `MediaStream` video elements remain native.
- 2026-08-16: replaced interpolated page-background CSS with `MediaBackground`.
  Cover video/image and repeated tenant skins validate through the shared state
  lifecycle; URLs no longer enter generated style text, and decorative
  backgrounds/watermarks are removed from the accessibility tree.
- 2026-08-16: finalized enforcement with only six reviewed ownership paths: the
  two shared media primitives, `UserAvatar`, bundled Bible art, `MediaStream`
  playback/capture, and Markdown HTML adapted by `RichTextRenderer`.

### Verification
- 2026-08-16: 14 focused primitive, rich-text, and article-feed tests pass.
- 2026-08-16: 11 page renderer/parity/frame tests pass.
- 2026-08-16: 9 focused upload, inbox, preview, scraper, product, media-table,
  and cart failure/interaction tests pass.
- 2026-08-16: media and native-dialog enforcement, Biome lint, all 181 frontend
  tests, TypeScript,
  production build, and `git diff --check` pass. Vite reports only the existing
  large-chunk advisory.
- 2026-08-16: affected-scope source/test audit covered empty/loading/error/URL
  replacement, fixed-frame mobile geometry, light/dark token usage, reduced
  motion, modal keyboard/focus behavior, media controls, and parent actions. A
  real-browser network-throttling matrix was unavailable in this repository
  environment; deterministic lifecycle/error tests provide the automated gate.

### Next Steps
- None. All planned phases and repository-executable verification are complete.

